  |title Saliency falls out naturally by recency and frequency

  |quote
    " recurrence does the triage for you, later, for free" ! yes, there's some of the magic-- we stay "consciously habitual" about being deliberately uncertain about things and ok with carrying them, and we get to *enjoy* recognizing uncertainties even earlier in the session that we hadn't realized at the time as we gain more experience, and that counterbalances the natural gravity toward thoughtless task-completion, and *saliency* falls out naturally by recency and frequency! Beautiful.

  |occasion
    On why carrying uncertainties forward is affordable rather than burdensome.

  |about
    A recorded question accrues a count, and the count does the triage later, for
    free. This is what makes assume-you-are-wrong sustainable rather than
    paralysing.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You have an uncertainty you are about to drop because it is not actionable.
    - A question just came up that you have seen before this session.

  |see
    (none recorded yet)
